C03: the plan boundary admits the process listing as producer of a text file (FILES1707)

In FILES1705 the mind proposed the mission system.process.list then filesystem.write.text with the write's arguments deferred to the verified listing, and the Kernel's plan boundary rejected it: filesystem.write.text had no permitted producer family. MissionPlanProposal now lists system.process.list as its producer. The App's plan observation projector keeps the listing's processes with their names and measures (workingSetBytes, cpuUsagePercent, totalProcessorSeconds), and before executing a deferred write it verifies that every line after the header is an observed process name followed by one of that listing's observed measures, exactly as the producer returned them — the write's authority is that projection, not a copied identity.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>


